{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"Good, the current best is 0.461 ratio. Let me understand what optimizations are already in place and what we can improve. Let me study the existing solution and think about what can be made faster.\n\nThe current solution:\n1. Computes q, k, v via reshaped matmul (good - replaces einsum)\n2. Computes logits via q@k^T\n3. Computes p0 via softmax\n4. For alpha != 1: computes p1 via symmetric softmax, then uses Gram matrix trick for norms\n5. Uses `p_mix @ v` for output\n\nKey operations: 3x q/k/v projections, 1x qk^T matmul, 2x softmax, 1x Gram G=xx^T, 3x p@something matmuls (p0@v, p1@G, pmix@G), 1x p_mix@v\n\nLet me check the input sizes and the case shapes:"}}
