{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_21","type":"agent_message","text":"Interesting - when logits comes from a fresh matmul, 4D softmax is 6.8ms and 2D view is 6.6ms. But earlier I measured 24.8ms for 4D softmax on a tensor created with `torch.randn(1, 20, 256, 256)`!\n\nWait no, that was with `x4 = torch.randn(1, 20, 256, 256)` giving 24.8ms. Let me re-check that.\n\nActually the difference is:\n- `torch.randn(1, 20, 256, 256).softmax(dim=-1)` → 24.8ms\n- `(q @ k.T).softmax(dim=-1)` → 6.8ms\n\nThat's very strange. Maybe the randn tensor has a different memory layout? Or maybe it's a different memory alignment issue.\n\nWait - actually, no. Let me re-read my earlier test:\n\n```\n4D softmax (1,20,256,256): 24.810 ms\n```\n\nBut now:\n```\n4D softmax: 6.773 ms\n```\n\nBoth are (1,20,256,256) contiguous. The difference might be in the loop count (20 iterations vs something else)? No, both were 20 iterations.\n\nHmm, maybe it's memory alignment, or maybe the first test had some issue. Let me redo the test more carefully.\n\nActually, I think the issue might be that in the earlier test, the tensor was one created by `torch.randn` vs one created by matmul. Maybe the matmul output is better aligned.\n\nWait no, that's unlikely. Let me just re-run the comparison carefully.\nInteresting! The softmax speed varies a lot by tensor origin. Let me understand this better and then build an optimized version.\n\nLet me first build an improved version with several optimizations and test it locally before running the full evaluation.\n\nKey optimizations to try:\n1. Stack QKV projections into one matmul\n2. Compute G = xx^T earlier (overlap with other computations mentally)\n3. Fuse the ratio computation\n4. Use torch.bmm with views for better performance\n5. Ensure optimal memory layouts\n\nLet me write an improved solution:\n"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_22","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python << 'EOF'\nimport torch, time, math\n\ntorch.set_num_threads(1)\ntorch.set_num_interop_threads(1)\n\nB, L, C, H, D = 1, 256, 1280, 20, 64\nalpha, beta = 1.05, 7.5\n\ntorch.manual_seed(42)\nx = torch.randn(B, L, C)\nwq = torch.randn(H, D, C)\nwk = torch.randn(H, D, C)\nwv = torch.randn(H, D, C)\n\n# Reference implementation (current solution)\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef attention_ref(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta):\n    B, L, C = x.shape\n    H, D = wq.shape[0], wq.shape[1]\n    inv_sqrt_d = 1.0 / math.sqrt(D)\n    HD = H * D\n    BHL = B * H * L\n    xr = x.reshape(B * L, C)\n\n    q = (xr @ wq.reshape(HD, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    k = (xr @ wk.reshape(HD, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    v = (xr @ wv.reshape(HD, C).T).reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n\n    logits = q @ k.transpose(-1, -2)\n    logits.mul_(inv_sqrt_d)\n\n    p0 = logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L)\n\n    if alpha == 1.0:\n        y = p0 @ v\n    else:\n        a_p = 0.5 * (1.0 + alpha)\n        a_m = 0.5 * (1.0 - alpha)\n        p1_logits = logits.mul(a_p)\n        p1_logits.add_(logits.transpose(-1, -2), alpha=a_m)\n        p1 = p1_logits.view(BHL, L).softmax(dim=-1).view(B, H, L, L)\n\n        p_mix = torch.lerp(p0, p1, beta)\n\n        G = x @ x.transpose(-1, -2)\n        G_exp = G.unsqueeze(1)\n\n        p1G = p1 @ G_exp\n        norm1_sq = p1G.mul_(p1).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n        pmG = p_mix @ G_exp\n        normm_sq = pmG.mul_(p_mix).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n        norm1 = norm1_sq.sqrt_().clamp_min_(1e-6)\n        normm = normm_sq.sqrt_().clamp_min_(1e-6)\n        ratio = norm1.div_(normm).clamp_(0.25, 4.0)\n\n        y = (p_mix @ v).mul_(ratio)\n\n    return y.transpose(1, 2).flatten(2).contiguous()\n\n# Benchmark reference\ny_ref = attention_ref(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\nfor _ in range(3):\n    attention_ref(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\nt0 = time.process_time_ns()\nfor _ in range(5):\n    y = attention_ref(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\nt1 = time.process_time_ns()\nprint(f'Reference: {(t1-t0)/5/1e6:.2f} ms')\n\n# New version: stacked QKV, bmm, other optimizations\n@torch.no_grad()\ndef attention_v2(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta):\n    B, L, C = x.shape\n    H, D = wq.shape[0], wq.shape[1]\n    inv_sqrt_d = 1.0 / math.sqrt(D)\n    HD = H * D\n    BH = B * H\n    BHL = BH * L\n\n    xr = x.reshape(B * L, C)\n\n    # Stack QKV projections into one matmul\n    w_qkv = torch.cat([wq.reshape(HD, C), wk.reshape(HD, C), wv.reshape(HD, C)], dim=0)\n    qkv = xr @ w_qkv.T\n    q_flat, k_flat, v_flat = qkv.split([HD, HD, HD], dim=1)\n\n    # Reshape to (B, H, L, D)\n    q = q_flat.reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    k = k_flat.reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n    v = v_flat.reshape(B, L, H, D).permute(0, 2, 1, 3).contiguous()\n\n    # Use bmm for logits\n    q_b = q.reshape(BH, L, D)\n    k_b = k.reshape(BH, L, D)\n    v_b = v.reshape(BH, L, D)\n\n    logits = torch.bmm(q_b, k_b.transpose(1, 2))\n    logits.mul_(inv_sqrt_d)\n\n    p0 = logits.softmax(dim=-1)\n\n    if alpha == 1.0:\n        y = torch.bmm(p0, v_b)\n    else:\n        a_p = 0.5 * (1.0 + alpha)\n        a_m = 0.5 * (1.0 - alpha)\n        # Fuse symmetric logits computation\n        p1_logits = logits.mul(a_p)\n        p1_logits.add_(logits.transpose(1, 2), alpha=a_m)\n        p1 = p1_logits.softmax(dim=-1)\n\n        # Compute p_mix in-place\n        p_mix = p0.clone()\n        p_mix.lerp_(p1, beta)\n\n        # G = x @ x\"'^T (B, L, L)\n        G = x @ x.transpose(-1, -2)\n\n        # For norms: use bmm with G broadcast\n        # p1 @ G: (BH, L, L) @ (B, L, L) - need to expand G\n        G_exp = G.expand(BH, L, L)\n        p1G = torch.bmm(p1, G_exp)\n        norm1_sq = p1G.mul_(p1).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n\n        pmG = torch.bmm(p_mix, G_exp)\n        normm_sq = pmG.mul_(p_mix).sum(dim=-1, keepdim=True)\n\n        norm1 = norm1_sq.sqrt_().clamp_min_(1e-6)\n        normm = normm_sq.sqrt_().clamp_min_(1e-6)\n        ratio = norm1.div_(normm).clamp_(0.25, 4.0)\n\n        y = torch.bmm(p_mix, v_b).mul_(ratio)\n\n    return y.reshape(B, H, L, D).transpose(1, 2).flatten(2).contiguous()\n\n# Correctness check\ny_v2 = attention_v2(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\nprint(f'\"'V2 max error: {(y_v2 - y_ref).abs().max():.2e}')\n\nfor _ in range(3):\n    attention_v2(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\nt0 = time.process_time_ns()\nfor _ in range(5):\n    y = attention_v2(x, wq, wk, wv, alpha, beta)\nt1 = time.process_time_ns()\nprint(f'V2: {(t1-t0)/5/1e6:.2f} ms')\nEOF\n\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
