{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_72","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/sh -lc \"python << 'PYEOF'\nimport torch, time, math\n\ntorch.set_num_threads(1)\ntorch.set_num_interop_threads(1)\n\nB, L, C, H, D = 1, 256, 1280, 20, 64\nalpha, beta = 1.05, 7.5\nHD = H * D\nBH = B * H\nBHL = BH * L\n\ntorch.manual_seed(42)\nx = torch.randn(B, L, C) / math.sqrt(C)\n\n# Time xx\"'^T\ndef xxT():\n    return x @ x.transpose(-1, -2)\nfor _ in range(3):\n    xxT()\nn = 20\nt0 = time.process_time_ns()\nfor _ in range(n):\n    xxT()\nt1 = time.process_time_ns()\nprint(f'\"'xx\"'^T: {(t1-t0)/n/1e6:.3f} ms'\"')\n\n# Time outer product sum approach?\n# sum of outer products = xx\"'^T, same thing.\n\n# What about: compute only upper triangle and symmetrize?\n# Probably slower.\n\n# Let'\"'s check: 2*xx\"'^T is the cost. Could we compute G = xx''^T more efficiently?\n# No, it'\"'s a standard BLAS syrk operation which PyTorch probably doesn't use.\n\n# Check if matmul with transpose is optimized\ndef xtx():\n    return x.T @ x  # (C, L) @ (L, C) = (C, C) - wrong shape\n# No, we need (L, C) @ (C, L) = (L, L) = xx\"'^T\n\n# This is already the standard form.\nPYEOF\n'","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
